A command whose main.go writes a two-byte character before an inline line
directive on one line. The rendered column of t counts only the bytes after the
directive, all ASCII, so t is reported at main.go:30:45.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() { println(s) }

var s = "é"; /*line main.go:30:40*/ var t = 1
